    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "The inclusion criteria were: (1) Conformed to research questions, i.e., studies that estimated the reinfection rate of SARS-CoV-2 or we could calculate it based on the data provided in the paper; (2) The study design included cohort study, case-control study, and descriptive study; (3) The study fited our working definition of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection... reinfection working definition in this study was based on a positive laboratory result at least 90 days after laboratory confirmation of primary infection",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies study designs, question framework components, and follow-up requirements (90-day interval) within the inclusion criteria."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "To avoid language bias, the search was not limited to any language... (4) Grey literature, including a range of documents not controlled by commercial publishing organizations.",
      "reason": "Language and publication status (grey literature) are specified, but dissemination year is not mentioned in the eligibility criteria."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "Therefore, we excluded the above literature with the number of unreported infections... Reports excluded: ... the number of first infections was not reported",
      "reason": "The review excludes studies with unreported outcomes but does not distinguish this from studies where outcomes were not measured."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "Subgroup analyses were performed by meta-regression to fit stratified rates of reinfection based on variables such as variant and country... we also used spline regression to fit time-varying reinfection rates",
      "reason": "Synthesis groups (variant, country, time) are specified and align with the review objectives (regions, populations, time trends)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "reinfection working definition in this study was based on a positive laboratory result at least 90 days... advised from WHO and US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention",
      "reason": "Rationale is provided for the reinfection definition restriction, but no rationale is provided for the sample size (<20) exclusion criterion."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 85
}

